# Combining Multiple-Choice and Constructed-Response Test Scores: An Economist's View.

**Authors:** Kennedy, Peter, Walstad, William B.

## Abstract
The consequences in terms of misclassifications of students that would occur by replacing the constructed-response portion of the Advanced Placement (AP) examinations in economics with more multiple-choice items were studied. The 1991 AP examinations in micro- and macroeconomics were used. Computer simulation found that a small but statistically significant number of misclassifications resulted. (SLD)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ553101

